onumber\,, \end{eqnarray} therefore, since $ rac 1{N_1} \log \left(|S_{R\sqrt{N_1}}| /\sqrt{2\pi}^{N_1} ight) 	o \log R + rac 1 2$ and thanks to Lemma ef{lemma-gusci} $$ \lim\sup_{N_1,N_2} rac1{N_1+N_2} \log Z_{N_1,N_2}( eta,\alpha,R)\leq \alpha q R^2 - rac \alpha2\intho_{MP}(\lambda;\alpha)\log(2q- eta(1-\alpha)\lambda)-\alpha\log R- rac\alpha2=:	ilde A(q)\,, $$ whence, as $	ilde A(q)$ is continuous, $$ \lim\sup_{N_1,N_2} rac{1}{N_1+N_2} \log Z_{N_1,N_2}( eta,\alpha,R)\leq\min_{2q\geq eta(1-\alpha)\lambda_+}	ilde A(q). $$ Moreover for $2q> eta(1-\alpha)\lambda_+$ $$ \partial_q^2 	ilde A(q)=2\alpha\int d\lambda rac{ho_{MP}(\lambda;\alpha)}{(2q- eta(1-\alpha)\lambda)^2}>0, $$ thus $	ilde A(q)$ is convex and the minimum is attained in a unique point $ ar q$. 
oindent Now the reverse bound. Let $\varepsilon>0$ and $S^c_{N_1,R,\varepsilon}$ the complementary set of the shell $S_{N_1,R,\varepsilon}$. It holds $$ \varepsilon \widehat Z_{N_1,N_2,\varepsilon}=e^{ q R^2 N_1} rac{(2\pi)^{ rac {N_1}{2}}}{|S_{R\sqrt{N_1}}|}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{N_1}} rac{dz}{(2\pi)^{ rac {N_1}{2}}} e^{-\sum_i^{N_1}(q- rac{ eta(1-\alpha)}{2}\lambda_i)z_i^2}-e^{ q R^2 N_1} rac{(2\pi)^{ rac N2}}{|S_{R\sqrt{N_1}}|}\int_{S_{N_1,R,\varepsilon}^c} rac{dz}{(2\pi)^{ rac {N_1}2}} e^{-\sum_i^{N_1}(q- rac{ eta(1-\alpha)}{2}\lambda_i)z_i^2}. $$ For any $\eta>0$ small enough we have  egin{eqnarray} \int_{S_{N_1,R,\varepsilon}^c} rac{dz}{(2\pi)^{ rac {N_1}2}} e^{-\sum_i^{N_1}(q- rac{ eta(1-\alpha)}{2}\lambda_i)z_i^2}&\leq&\exp\left[N_1\left(\eta\left(R^2- rac\varepsilon {N_1}ight)- rac{1}{2N_1}\sum_j\log(2q- eta\lambda_j+2\eta)ight)ight]
onumber\ &+&\exp\left[N_1\left(-\eta\left(R^2+ rac\varepsilon {N_1}ight)- rac{1}{2N_1}\sum_j\log(2q- eta\lambda_j-2\eta)ight)ight]
onumber. \end{eqnarray} 
oindent Note now that the r.h.s. is $o(e^{-N})$ if $ rac\varepsilon N	o\infty$ as $N	o\infty$. So the greatest contribution is at the scale $\varepsilon=	ilde\varepsilon N$, $	ilde\varepsilon>0$ independent on $N_1$. Therefore  egin{equation} \lim\inf_{N_1,N_2}\widehat A_{N_1,N_2,	ilde\varepsilon}\geq\max\left(	ilde A(q), A^1_{	ilde\varepsilon}(\eta; q), A^2_{	ilde\varepsilon}(\eta; q)ight), \end{equation} with  egin{eqnarray} A^1_{	ilde\varepsilon}(\eta; q)&=&\alpha(q+\eta)R^2-\alpha	ilde\varepsilon\eta- rac\alpha2\int d\lambdaho_{MP}(\lambda;\alpha)\log(2(q+\eta)- eta\lambda)-\alpha\log R- rac\alpha2;\ A^2_{	ilde\varepsilon}(\eta; q)&=&\alpha(q-\eta)R^2-\alpha	ilde\varepsilon\eta- rac\alpha2\int d\lambdaho_{MP}(\lambda;\alpha)\log(2(q-\eta)- eta\lambda)-\alpha\log R- rac\alpha2. \end{eqnarray} Now we show that if $ ar q$ is the unique minimiser of $	ilde A(q)$ it is for $\eta$ small enough $$ 	ilde A( ar q)=\max\left(	ilde A( ar q), A^1_{	ilde\varepsilon}(\eta;  ar q), A^2_{	ilde\varepsilon}(\eta;  ar q)ight)\,, $$ which will conclude the proof. To do so we introduce  egin{eqnarray} \Delta_-(q;\eta)&:=&	ilde A(q)-A^1_{	ilde\varepsilon}(\eta; q)= -\alpha\eta(R^2-	ilde\varepsilon)+ rac\alpha2\int d\lambdaho_{MP}(\lambda;\alpha)\log\left( rac{2(q+\eta)- eta\lambda}{2q- eta\lambda}ight);\ \Delta_+(q;\eta)&:=&	ilde A(q)-A^2_{	ilde\varepsilon}(\eta; q)= \alpha\eta(R^2+	ilde\varepsilon)+ rac\alpha2\int d\lambdaho_{MP}(\lambda;\alpha)\log\left( rac{2(q-\eta)- eta\lambda}{2q- eta\lambda}ight)\,. \end{eqnarray} 
oindent As a function of $\eta$, $\Delta_\pm(q;\eta)$ are continuous and differentiable, vanishing in $\eta=0$ and with $\lim_{\eta	o+\infty}\Delta_\pm(q,\eta)=\pm\infty$. Moreover $\Delta_+(q;\eta)$ is uniformly convex and $\Delta_-(q;\eta)$ uniformly concave. Thus $\Delta_-(q;\eta)$ assumes a positive maximum iff the derivative in $\eta=0$ is positive, that is  egin{equation} 0<-(R^2-	ilde\varepsilon)+\int d\lambda rac{ho_{MP}(\lambda;\alpha)}{2q- eta\lambda}=	ilde \varepsilon-\partial_q 	ilde A(q)\,. \end{equation} 
